---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Container from "../components/common/Container.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | DevOps4Solutions" description="About Nidhi Gupta and DevOps4Solutions.">
 	<Container className="py-14">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">About DevOps4Solutions</h1>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-950">Building Enterprise Cloud Platforms That Scale</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        DevOps4Solutions was founded by <strong>Nidhi Gupta</strong>, a Lead Platform DevOps Engineer with over <strong>16 years of experience </strong>
         designing, automating, and modernizing enterprise cloud platforms. The mission is simple: transform complex cloud and DevOps
        challenges into practical, scalable, and production-ready solutions.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        Throughout my career, I have worked in multiple enterprise organizations to architect highly available, secure, and automated AWS
        platforms that accelerate software delivery while maintaining operational excellence. Rather than focusing only on deploying
        infrastructure, I help organizations build cloud foundations that remain reliable, compliant, and easy to operate as they grow.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        My expertise spans the complete cloud platform lifecycle—from architecture and migration to automation, security, platform
        engineering, and continuous improvement.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-950">Why DevOps4Solutions?</h3>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        Technology evolves rapidly, but many organizations continue to struggle with cloud complexity, inconsistent automation, technical
        debt, and operational challenges. DevOps4Solutions was created to assist devops engineers bridge the gap between theoretical best practices and real-world
        enterprise implementation.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        Every article, architecture diagram, tutorial, and video shared through DevOps4Solutions is based on practical experience gained
        from designing and operating production cloud environments. The goal is not simply to explain AWS services, but to demonstrate how
        they work together to build secure, scalable, resilient, and maintainable enterprise platforms.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        Whether you're beginning your cloud journey or modernizing an existing enterprise environment, DevOps4Solutions provides practical
        guidance that helps engineering teams make informed architectural decisions with confidence.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-950">Our Mission</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        To empower engineers, architects, and organizations by providing practical cloud architecture guidance, automation frameworks, and
        real-world DevOps solutions that enable teams to build secure, scalable, resilient, and operationally excellent cloud platforms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-950">Our Philosophy</h2>
      
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">Our guiding principles are simple:</p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        <li><strong>Design for scale from the beginning.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Automate everything that can be automated.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Prioritize security and compliance as foundational requirements.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Build resilient, observable, and operationally reliable systems.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Use proven architectural patterns instead of unnecessary complexity.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Continuously modernize through incremental improvements rather than disruptive rewrites.</strong></li>
      </ul>
     
    </article>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>
